{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "חלום", :translit "chalom", :gloss "a dream"} {:he "בנבואה", :translit "bin'vu'ah", :gloss "in prophecy"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "חלום", :b "בנבואה"}], :frame {:text "Jacob's dream at Bethel is treated by the Rabbis as a prophetic vision, not an ordinary dream. The Talmud states that all dreams follow their interpretation, and dreams are classed as a lower form of prophecy; the Sages refer to dreams as a sixtieth of prophecy (Berakhot 55b, 57b).", :sources ["Berakhot 55b" "Berakhot 57b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "סולם", :translit "sulam", :gloss "ladder"} {:he "כסא הכבוד", :translit "kisei ha-kavod", :gloss "the Throne of Glory"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "סולם", :b "כסא הכבוד"}], :frame {:text "The heavenly Throne of Glory is described in Ezekiel's vision as God's seat (Ezekiel 1:26). The identification of Jacob's ladder with the Throne of Glory links the Bethel vision to the divine chariot and throne imagery.", :sources ["Ezekiel 1:26"]}} {:quotes [{:he "סולם", :translit "sulam", :gloss "ladder"} {:he "קול", :translit "kol", :gloss "voice"} {:he "ממון", :translit "mamon", :gloss "money"} {:he "עוני", :translit "oni", :gloss "poverty"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "סולם", :b "קול"} {:kind :gematria, :a "סולם", :b "ממון"} {:kind :gematria, :a "סולם", :b "עוני"}], :frame {:text "The Rabbis interpret Jacob's ladder as symbolizing prayer, the substitute for sacrifice after the Temple's destruction. Hosea calls prayer a 'bull of the lips,' equating prayer with sacrificial offerings (Hosea 14:3). The Talmud states that prayer stands in the place of the daily offerings (Berakhot 26b). The angel ascending in the flame of Manoah's offering (Judges 13:20) is cited as a parallel to angels ascending the ladder.", :sources ["Hosea 14:3" "Berakhot 26b" "Judges 13:20"]}} {:quotes [{:he "סלם", :translit "sulam", :gloss "ladder"} {:he "סמל", :translit "semel", :gloss "image / symbol"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The letters of סלם rearrange as סמל, an anagram."}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "והנה סלם", :translit "vehineh sulam", :gloss "and behold a ladder"} {:he "וקץ", :translit "vakeitz", :gloss "and the end"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "והנה סלם", :b "וקץ"}], :frame {:text "The Midrash states that God showed Jacob the end of the four exiles, including the ultimate keitz (end) promised to Daniel: 'Blessed is he who waits and reaches the keitz' (Daniel 12:12). Genesis Rabbah records that God showed Jacob the kingdoms that would subjugate his descendants (Bereshit Rabbah 68:12).", :sources ["Daniel 12:12" "Bereshit Rabbah 68:12"]}} {:quotes [{:he "סלם", :translit "sulam", :gloss "ladder"} {:he "סיני", :translit "sinai", :gloss "Sinai"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "סלם", :b "סיני"}], :frame {:text "The Midrash interprets the ladder as foreshadowing Mount Sinai. The numerical equivalence of סולם and סיני supports the rabbinic reading that God showed Jacob the revelation at Sinai, where the Torah was given (Exodus 19). Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer connects the ladder to Sinai.", :sources ["Exodus 19" "Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer ch. 35"]}} {:quotes [{:he "סלם מוצב", :translit "sulam mutzav", :gloss "a ladder set up"} {:he "מרכבו", :translit "merkavo", :gloss "His chariot"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "סלם מוצב", :b "מרכבו"}], :frame {:text "Ezekiel's vision of the divine Chariot (מרכבה) is the foundational prophetic text for the heavenly realm (Ezekiel 1:4–28). The linkage of the ladder to God's chariot places Jacob's vision within the merkavah tradition.", :sources ["Ezekiel 1:4–28"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מוצב", :translit "mutzav", :gloss "set up / stationed"} {:he "אלון מוצב אשר בשכם", :translit "elon mutzav asher bishkhem", :gloss "the oak of Moreh that is by Shechem"} {:he "וצרתי עליך מוצב", :translit "v'tzarti aleikh mutzav", :gloss "and I will encamp against you a siege"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["מוצב" "אלון מוצב אשר בשכם" "וצרתי עליך מוצב"]}], :frame {:text "Jacob's first encampment upon returning to the land is at Shechem (Genesis 33:18). The Midrash notes that Shechem was the first conquest in the land and also the site of later tribulation (Bereshit Rabbah 79:7). The siege word מוצב is used in military contexts (e.g., Numbers 31:6, הצבא המוצב).", :sources ["Genesis 33:18" "Bereshit Rabbah 79:7"]}} {:quotes [{:he "סלם", :translit "sulam", :gloss "ladder"} {:he "למס", :translit "lemas", :gloss "imposed tribute / dispossession"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The letters of סלם rearrange as למס, an anagram."}], :frame {:text "The word למס appears in the Torah describing the imposition of forced labor (Deuteronomy 20:11). It is linked by the Rabbis to the subjugation of Israel during the exiles.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 20:11"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והנה סולם מוצב", :translit "vehineh sulam mutzav", :gloss "and behold a ladder set up"} {:he "הכבש", :translit "ha-kevesh", :gloss "the ramp"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "והנה סולם מוצב", :b "הכבש"}], :frame {:text "The ramp (כבש) of the altar is described in the instructions for the bronze altar (Exodus 27:8, Ezekiel 43:17). The Temple's altar had a ramp rather than steps per Exodus 20:23. The ladder set on earth is thus linked to the altar's ramp by which priests ascend.", :sources ["Exodus 20:23" "Exodus 27:8" "Ezekiel 43:17"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ארצה", :translit "artzah", :gloss "to the earth / groundward"} {:he "מזבח אדמה", :translit "mizbeiach adamah", :gloss "altar of earth"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word association: ארצה hints at מזבח אדמה."}], :frame {:text "Exodus 20:21–22 commands: 'An altar of earth (מזבח אדמה) you shall make for Me.' The Ba'al HaTurim reads 'groundward' in the ladder vision as an allusion to this earthen altar.", :sources ["Exodus 20:21–22"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וראשו מגיע השמימה", :translit "v'rosho magei'a ha-shamayma", :gloss "and its top reaching heavenward"} {:he "והנה סלם", :translit "vehineh sulam", :gloss "and behold a ladder"} {:he "וזה מזבח העולה", :translit "vazeh mizbeiach ha-olah", :gloss "and this is the altar of the burnt offering"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "והנה סלם", :b "וזה מזבח העולה"}], :frame {:text "The fragrance of sacrifices ascending to heaven is described in the Torah: 'a pleasing fragrance to the Lord' (e.g., Genesis 8:21, Leviticus 1:9). The burnt offering altar is detailed in Exodus 27:1–8. The Midrash explicitly identifies Jacob's ladder with the altar, since Bethel is where Jacob later builds one (Genesis 35:7).", :sources ["Genesis 8:21" "Leviticus 1:9" "Exodus 27:1–8" "Genesis 35:7"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והנה מלאכי", :translit "vehineh mal'achei", :gloss "and behold angels of"} {:he "אלו הכהנים", :translit "elu ha-kohanim", :gloss "these are the priests"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The letters of והנה מלאכי rearrange as אלו הכהנים, an anagram."}], :frame {:text "The priests minister at the altar, ascending and descending the ramp (כבש) as prescribed in Temple service. The Talmud describes the daily service of the priests in tractate Yoma, including their assigned tasks in the Temple (Yoma 25b–33a). The equation of angels with priests draws on Malachi 2:7, where the priest is called 'messenger (מלאך) of the Lord of Hosts.'", :sources ["Malachi 2:7" "Yoma 25b"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מוצב ארצה וראשו מגיע השמימה", :translit "mutzav artzah v'rosho magei'a ha-shamayma", :gloss "set on the earth and its top reaching heavenward"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading of the phrase as an aphorism about the fallen who rise again."}], :frame {:text "The Rabbis understand the ladder as a paradigm of divine mercy: one cast down is not abandoned, for the ladder spans earth to heaven. Psalms expresses this: 'When I fall, I shall arise' (Micah 7:8); 'The Lord lifts up the downtrodden' (Psalms 146:8).", :sources ["Micah 7:8" "Psalms 146:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מלאכי אלהים", :translit "mal'chei elohim", :gloss "angels of God"} {:he "ויפגעו [בו] מלאכי אלהים", :translit "va-yifg'u [bo] mal'chei elohim", :gloss "and [he] encountered angels of God"} {:he "מלאכי אלהים עולים", :translit "mal'chei elohim olim", :gloss "angels of God ascending"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["מלאכי אלהים" "ויפגעו מלאכי אלהים"]}], :frame {:text "The Midrash (Bereshit Rabbah 68:12; Tanhuma Vayeitzei 2) explains that the angels who accompanied Jacob within the Land of Israel were not permitted to leave it, and new angels descended to accompany him abroad. Thus the ascending angels are those of the Land completing their mission, and the descending ones are the outside-land angels taking over, whom Jacob encounters on his return in Genesis 32:2.", :sources ["Bereshit Rabbah 68:12" "Tanhuma Vayeitzei 2" "Genesis 32:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "עלים [ויורדים]", :translit "olim [v'yordim]", :gloss "ascending [and descending]"} {:he "בבל מדי יון ורומי", :translit "bavel madai yavan v'romi", :gloss "Babylon Media Greece and Rome"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "עלים [ויורדים]", :b "בבל מדי יון ורומי"}], :frame {:text "The four exiles — Babylon, Media-Persia, Greece, and Rome (Edom) — are a standard rabbinic framework. Daniel's visions successively depict these kingdoms (Daniel 2:37–40, 7:4–23). The Midrash applies them to Jacob's vision of the ladder, where the ascending and descending movements allude to the rise and fall of these empires (Bereshit Rabbah 68:12; Leviticus Rabbah 29:2 links the four kingdoms to Sukkot's four species).", :sources ["Daniel 2:37–40" "Daniel 7:4–23" "Bereshit Rabbah 68:12" "Leviticus Rabbah 29:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "חלום", :a-value 84, :b "בנבואה", :b-value 66, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "סולם", :a-value 136, :b "כסא הכבוד", :b-value 118, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "סולם", :a-value 136, :b "קול", :b-value 136, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "סולם", :a-value 136, :b "ממון", :b-value 136, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "סולם", :a-value 136, :b "עוני", :b-value 136, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "The letters of סלם rearrange as סמל, an anagram.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "והנה סלם", :a-value 196, :b "וקץ", :b-value 196, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "סלם", :a-value 130, :b "סיני", :b-value 130, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "סלם מוצב", :a-value 268, :b "מרכבו", :b-value 268, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["מוצב" "אלון מוצב אשר בשכם" "וצרתי עליך מוצב"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מוצב", :refs ["Genesis 28:12" "Joshua 4:9" "Judges 9:6" "1 Samuel 13:23" "1 Samuel 14:1" "1 Samuel 14:4" "1 Samuel 14:6" "1 Samuel 14:11"], :n 11, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "אלון מוצב אשר בשכם", :refs ["Judges 9:6"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "וצרתי עליך מוצב", :refs ["Isaiah 29:3"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :other, :note "The letters of סלם rearrange as למס, an anagram.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "והנה סולם מוצב", :a-value 340, :b "הכבש", :b-value 327, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Word association: ארצה hints at מזבח אדמה.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "והנה סלם", :a-value 196, :b "וזה מזבח העולה", :b-value 191, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "The letters of והנה מלאכי rearrange as אלו הכהנים, an anagram.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading of the phrase as an aphorism about the fallen who rise again.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["מלאכי אלהים" "ויפגעו מלאכי אלהים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מלאכי אלהים", :refs ["Genesis 28:12" "Genesis 32:2"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ויפגעו מלאכי אלהים", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "עלים [ויורדים]", :a-value 426, :b "בבל מדי יון ורומי", :b-value 416, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:09:33.607356604Z", :model "glm-5.2"}